# P18-V01 CreateTopicRequestHeader reflection decoding — 2026-10-18T00:25:52Z

- Repository: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`.
- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Pinned Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 at
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` in the read-only checkout
  `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq`.
- Source inspection confirmed `CreateTopicRequestHeader` does not implement
  `FastCodesHeader`. Both `useFastEncode` hints fall through to
  `RemotingCommand.decodeCommandCustomHeaderDirectly`'s reflection loop. Each
  field conversion exception is caught independently; nullable fields retain
  null/default state, Boolean parsing follows `Boolean.parseBoolean`, and
  `checkFields()` validates `topicFilterType` after all fields are visited.
- Rust now exposes the Java nullable/reference fields as `Option`, skips failed
  numeric field conversions for this header, preserves the initialized false
  values of `order` and `force`, and runs the final `topicFilterType` check.
  Producer/consumer topic-creation call sites and tests now pass explicit
  `Some` values. The invoked Java fixture covers both mode hints, valid values,
  missing/malformed numeric fields, malformed Boolean text, and valid/invalid/
  missing topic filter type. Fixture SHA-256:
  `20e0a1c2dd78af55b220976ad6faecc37673d0d6951954a4a0c2bc433a7053a7`.
- Implementation commit: `4f7f9435 fix(protocol): match create-topic reflection decode`.

